WEBVTT

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:04.030
This is for everyone's sake too

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.610
Howard took parts?

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.110
No doubt about it.

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:19.410
And that was definitely the Gyrostabilizer?

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:20.720
Well...

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.260
Damn Howard...

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:45.430
Bob, you should try some too.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.400
How long do we plan to stay here?

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:55.900
We should hurry up and find them
and take their Gyrostabilizer!

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.510
Don't be impatient, Bob.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.850
There's no doubt they're on this island.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:04.370
And that mechanic's probably with them.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:09.620
Which means they know
we're escaped prisoners.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:10.780
Yeah.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.160
But we don't know anything about them.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.520
Waiting around isn't bad
if it's for the sake of caution.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.550
That might be true, but...

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:21.580
And it seems to be a pretty fun planet.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.900
And the ship's totally locked down, so we don't have to worry about them taking it over.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:30.170
Since we just escaped, we have plenty
of time to enjoy ourselves for a while.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.170
Do what you want!

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:34.820
But anyways, where is this?

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:39.400
I never heard anything about a planet
like this being near colony B-3.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.200
Get out here, escaped prisoners!

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.450
I know you're in there!

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.300
Calm down, Howard.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.580
Don't let them pull you along at their pace.

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:56.420
Is it you who called us out?

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:01.110
Oh, I thought someone was there,
but it's just a little kid!

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.130
What do you want?

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:10.630
Good luck, Howard. You should be fine!

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:14.680
An exchange?

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:15.880
What do you mean?

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:17.720
Excuse me...

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.430
You messed it up.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:24.810
Don't rush it... you can't be impatient!

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:26.380
Hey, kid!

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:27.360
Bob.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:29.500
But this brat...

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:33.320
It's really calming to be here.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.460
Now, would you mind telling us what you meant?

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.760
I guess. You guys know, right?

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:47.910
That we're the students from Soria academy
who were shipwrecked during a school trip.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.630
You did tell us that, didn't you?

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.770
What about it?

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.350
Didn't you know?

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:56.830
That accident is well known
throughout the galaxy.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.030
Well known?

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.700
Come to think of it, I heard about it.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:05.270
The Howard Group put up a reward
for the safe return of his stupid son.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:06.850
Stupid son?

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.060
Then you're those...

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:11.910
Isn't there anyone else?

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:20.980
Yeah, us seven, a cheeky cat robot, and a child
of another species, plus the old mechanic.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:22.260
I see...

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:24.880
That old man was with you after all!

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.510
So? What's to be exchanged?

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:32.980
I heard from the old man that
your ship's Gyrostabilizer is broken.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:35.760
That guy, blabbing unnecessarily.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:39.920
We'll hand over our Gyrostabilizer.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:40.970
What?

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:46.410
But you take us back to our colony.
Those are the terms.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:49.970
If you take me home, you'll get
the reward money from my papa.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:51.850
Doesn't sound half-bad, does it?

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.200
'Everyone' is impossible.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.410
We don't have enough food.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.260
But here there's food...

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.470
He said it's impossible, so it's impossible!

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.750
But if it's just one person, we'll consider it.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:05.650
One person?

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:06.770
One person...

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.380
Everyone would be angry if only I went home.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:16.930
But once I was safe, I could get
Papa to send a search-and-rescue ship.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:20.420
So, how about it?

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.380
Fine. Take me along.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.000
I'll get help for the others.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.830
Will your friends be okay?

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.800
This is for everyone's sake too.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.580
Okay, then let's complete the exchange.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:36.580
Would you hand over the Gyrostabilizer?

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:39.620
Okay.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.470
With this, we can leave this planet whenever we want.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:50.310
So, we should hurry to your space ship...

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:51.550
Naive kid, aren't you?

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:53.950
What's the meaning of this?

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:57.660
Now that we have the Gyrostabilizer,
we have no need for you.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:00.170
This isn't what we agreed to!

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:03.250
If you take me home,
you'll get the reward money!

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.950
When I want money, I take it.

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:09.470
Wait a second! If it's not money you want, what else?

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:12.020
Freedom? That could be arranged.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:14.760
My Papa could make arrangements with the police.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.310
Really? That's impressive!

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:18.470
Wait!

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.200
It's not the Gyrostabilizer?

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:24.850
Are you sure?

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.230
There's no doubt.

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:27.550
That's ridiculous!

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:31.180
That old man definitely said it was the Gyrostabilizer!

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:34.070
It's definitely a part of the Gyrostabilizer...

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:35.650
...but it's just memory.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.220
We're fine without it.

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:38.870
Exactly.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:42.320
That idiot took the wrong thing with him!

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:49.070
Th... that's..

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:50.680
What should we do, Brindo?

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.030
We have no choice.

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:55.030
We'll have him show us the way to the space ship.

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:57.320
I can't do it!

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:01.150
If you show us the way, we'll take you alone back to the colony.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:02.760
You think you can trick me?

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:04.410
That's what you just said you'd do!

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:07.330
You're planning to kill me
once I show you the way!

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:09.580
Then we have no choice.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:15.400
Will you show us the way, or won't you?

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:18.730
Go save him?

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:22.150
They should also have realized
they can't use that part.

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:23.830
In which case, Howard is...

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:25.670
Give it up, give it up!

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:29.050
There's no need to save a traitor.

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:34.150
More importantly, we have to fix this
space ship and escape from this planet!

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.070
We can't just leave him alone!

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:38.200
What did you say?

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:41.610
First and foremost, he's our friend.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:45.320
Are you serious?

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:48.470
We certainly can't forgive his selfishness.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:51.170
But we can't stand idly by while he's killed.

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:54.360
He tried to save himself alone!

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.210
I'm sure he did it for everyone!

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:03.020
As long as Howard is of some value
to them, they probably won't kill him.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.010
We still have time.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:08.380
We know this island better than them.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:09.960
There must be something we can do!

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:14.500
They're escaped prisoners, and they have weapons!

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:16.000
We know that.

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:30.360
I guess I have no choice. I'll help you.

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:34.110
I know the most about them, after all.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.420
Mr. Porte!

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:37.710
As thanks for you saving me.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:40.970
In that case, we'd better plan our strategy.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.410
I have the map of the island.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:49.370
Hey, can you hear me?

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:53.010
If you hear me, answer.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.660
This voice is Brindo!

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:56.830
One of the escaped prisoners.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:59.050
It's the old mechanic!

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:02.680
Damn you, Gramps! You thought
you could escape on your own?

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:04.480
Damn straight I did!

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:06.880
Who'd want to stay with you bunch?

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:09.660
I'd have rather gone up in flames
with the transport ship!

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:11.460
What did you say?

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:14.800
Next time I see you I'll snap your bones like twigs!

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:16.560
If you think you can, then try!

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:18.770
It'll just give me a chance to take you out!

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:23.680
Ouch!

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.210
Serves you right!

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:29.350
So, what's your business?

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.270
We have the brat named Howard.

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:37.410
If you want us to return him,
bring us the real Gyrostabilizer.

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:40.330
What's your answer?

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:41.870
What should we do, Luna?

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:47.910
I see. I guess you don't care
what happens to this traitor.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:50.160
Very well.

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:54.770
But first, let us hear Howard's voice.

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:57.620
We need to confirm Howard's safety first.

00:10:57.620 --> 00:11:01.600
Fine. Hey, c'mere.
They say they want to hear your voice.

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:07.900
Luna, it's me--Howard! Forgive me,
I really meant for this to go better.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:10.070
But <i>these guys...</i>

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:11.800
Stop babbling!

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.050
How about I let them hear you scream in pain?

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:17.910
Hey, hey.

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:20.010
Scream a little louder!

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:27.430
Fine, that's enough!

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:31.110
Then I guess we've agreed on an exchange.

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:32.050
Not yet.

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:33.020
What?

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:36.170
We know that you have weapons.

00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:40.330
We can't just let you kill us
as soon as you have the Gyrostabilizer.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:42.850
We need a guarantee on our lives.

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.010
A guarantee?

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:48.700
Hey, all of you, do you even understand
the situation you've put yourselves in?

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:53.650
We should just kill the lot of you and take it!

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:55.650
What should we do, Brindo?

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:03.430
There will be no guarantee.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:07.030
We'll take our time hunting you out, so be prepared.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:08.500
Wait!

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:38.530
Very well. We'll trade.

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:44.720
The time: sunrise tomorrow. The place will be at the base of the waterfall in the eastern woods.

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:48.580
We'll exchange the Gyrostabilizer and Howard there.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:50.650
At the base of the waterfall?

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:55.330
Howard knows the place. It's where the rope hangs down.

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:04.710
Fine.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:08.080
But it's in all your best interests
not to play any strange tricks.

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:09.100
I know.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:10.630
See you later.

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:12.170
Look forward to it.

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:23.570
They don't even realize they'll be killed! What idiots!

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:25.780
You-- you're really going to kill them?

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.850
If we leave them alive, they might be a thorn in our side later.

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:33.280
Once we're done with them, we'll finish you off nice and slowly. Look forward to it.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:36.510
But is this okay, Brindo?

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:40.600
The base of the waterfall means they'll
definitely have something planned.

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:42.770
There's nothing to worry about.

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:46.900
They're a bunch of kids like him. What can they do?

00:13:57.170 --> 00:13:58.600
You're going alone?

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:02.270
If I use the cave under the waterfall,
I can sneak up behind them.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:04.450
You can't! It's too dangerous!

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:08.910
Howard may not have understood your message, Kaoru.

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:12.060
If they use the cave instead of
climbing down the rope, you're finished!

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:17.720
Maybe we should just hand it over honestly.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:24.400
Their objective is to fix their space ship.
Killing us won't accomplish anything.

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:25.410
You're naive.

00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:29.910
They don't need a reason to kill.
They kill because they like to.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:31.670
That's all there is to it.

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:36.960
And if we give them the Gyrostabilizer,
we won't be able to fly.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:38.530
But...

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:44.650
We can't give them the Gyrostabilizer.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:47.160
I'll go on my own after all.

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:51.320
Wait!

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:55.110
Wait, Kaoru!

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:58.600
You definitely can't go on your own.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:01.600
Think back, Kaoru.

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:05.730
Since we came to this planet, we've encountered many hardships...

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:09.610
...but we've always overcome them by working together!

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:12.210
If we work together this time...

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:14.080
They're not that generous.

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:17.720
And if worst comes to worst,
it's best that the fewest are sacrificed.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:22.000
Don't worry. I'll definitely save Howard.

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:29.080
Don't you understand yet?

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:32.310
There's someone who told you
something important, isn't there?

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:35.350
He wouldn't be happy if you did that.

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.820
"Live!" That's what he said!

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.930
Kaoru, let go!

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:46.750
If you don't, you'll die too!

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:55.110
Kaoru...

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:01.030
I leave my dream in your care.

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:05.050
Live!

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:11.950
Louis!

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:20.230
There must be something we can do.

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:22.330
Let's all think about it together!

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:26.270
Please, Kaoru!

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:45.470
I just can't go against you.

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:47.720
Kaoru.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:17.310
It's great to have a bed.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:32.950
A little further...

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:59.720
Don't try anything pointless.

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.880
I was so close!

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:20.570
Then I guess it's decided.

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:22.030
How about it, Kaoru?

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:23.610
No problem.

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.300
I wonder if it'll go well.

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:28.150
It's okay. I'm sure we'll succeed.

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:30.430
The rest is up to teamwork.

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:32.830
What should I do?

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:37.180
Adam, stay here with Sharla and help everyone.

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:40.150
I want to go with you!

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:43.780
You're still too small, Adam, and it's very dangerous.

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:45.020
But...

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:46.150
Adam...

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:50.570
We're leaving the gravity control unit to you.

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:55.560
Whether we rescue Howard safely or not, they'll eventually come here.

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:57.960
We'll just have to fix it by then.

00:18:58.260 --> 00:18:59.680
Leave it to us.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:02.080
Then we'd better get started.

00:19:02.270 --> 00:19:03.920
There's no time to waste!

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:16.560
If only I was strong too...

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:34.150
Just...

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:35.120
...a little...

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:37.330
...a little further...

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:39.580
Got it!

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:47.800
So? What were you trying to do?

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:51.850
I've very sorry it was nothing please forgive me.

00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:56.050
What's wrong?

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:58.630
I was just playing with the boy.

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:00.550
It's time we got going.

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:04.820
Let's go.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.650
Keep walking!

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:16.650
I know...

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.750
Looks good. Just like that.

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:31.000
How's it over there?

00:20:32.610 --> 00:20:34.450
What are you doing?

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:38.530
I was... connecting this circuit here.

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:40.220
Who told you to do that?

00:20:41.270 --> 00:20:44.680
If you don't bring this over here there's no point to it!

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:46.930
I see...

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.560
Don't you even know that much?

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:52.820
Where's the genius boy who took home the Gangaur Award?

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:55.520
They made a big deal of it in the news recently.

00:21:03.850 --> 00:21:05.500
You can do the rest, right?

00:21:06.060 --> 00:21:06.770
Yes.

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:17.950
They don't seem to have arrived yet.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:24.510
They're here!

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:29.980
Howard...

00:21:32.230 --> 00:21:33.280
What?

00:21:35.380 --> 00:21:37.300
What's up with these big plants?

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:40.330
This planet never gets boring.

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:41.760
This way.

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:48.250
He's heading for the cave!

00:21:48.810 --> 00:21:51.280
I guess he didn't figure it out after all.

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:56.720
Even with a rope, can we climb down this?

00:21:57.400 --> 00:21:58.370
Rope?

00:21:58.820 --> 00:22:02.460
Howard knows the place. It's where the rope hangs down.

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:04.970
What's wrong?

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:08.120
I just got turned around a little.

00:22:08.980 --> 00:22:10.480
It's over here.

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:12.660
Get with it!

00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:14.650
They're heading for the rope.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:17.010
Howard figured it out!

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:20.120
Well then, we should proceed according to plan.

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:05.910
Howard, wait! We'll save you soon!

00:23:06.060 --> 00:23:07.750
Leave the exchange to me!

00:23:08.200 --> 00:23:10.260
We won't abandon you!

00:23:10.710 --> 00:23:12.360
We'll definitely save you...

00:23:12.960 --> 00:23:15.960
That's right. We're friends, after all.

00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:18.250
Everyone... come home safely...

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:19.820
I'll be sniffin' and prayin' for you!

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:28.070
Next time: I finally also...
